    L.append("2. Leakage controls and inputs, applied before any job.")
    L.append(f"- Training pairs come from the Drug Interactions sections of SemEval vocabulary drugs by `ddiood.ood.build_pairs` (the 14 anchor tokens, partner-matched negatives that the anchor's label never names, 2 negatives per positive, at most 10 positives per anchor, seed 42). Anchors pass `label_identity` (`ddiood/ood.py:93-103`: {c['anchor_gate_rejections'].get('label_identity:combination_product_label', 0)} combination labels and {c['anchor_gate_rejections'].get('label_identity:label_is_for_another_moiety', 0)} other-moiety labels rejected). A vocabulary drug is treated as equivalent to an OOD drug, and excluded as anchor and as partner, if its name, canonical name, RxCUI or label ingredient equals one, if one is a whole-word part of the other, or if their salt-stripped core names (at least 6 characters) contain one another in either direction; this catches prodrugs and active metabolites such as aprepitant and fosaprepitant, naltrexone and methylnaltrexone, somatropin and lonapegsomatropin-tcgd, venlafaxine and desvenlafaxine, sirolimus and temsirolimus. {c['anchor_gate_rejections'].get('excluded_ood_equivalent_or_ingredient_overlap', 0)} otherwise eligible anchors are rejected that way and {c['anchors_after_gates']} anchors remain.")
    L.append(f"- Built {c['built_pairs']} pairs ({c['built_positives']} positive). Dropped: {d.get('ood_drug_as_anchor', 0)} pairs with an OOD drug as anchor, {d.get('ood_drug_as_partner', 0)} pairs with an OOD drug (or a vocabulary drug equivalent to one) as partner, {d.get('unordered_pair_in_ood_set', 0)} pairs whose unordered pair is in either OOD set, {d.get('duplicate_unordered_pair', 0)} reversed duplicates, {d.get('negative_reverse_mention', 0)} negatives whose partner's label names the anchor, {d.get('negative_conflicts_with_positive', 0)} negatives that conflict with a positive. Final training set: {c['final_pairs']} pairs, {c['final_positives']} positive and {c['final_negatives']} negative, {c['anchor_drugs']} anchors, {c['partner_drugs']} partners; hash `{man['train_hash']}`. {c['excluded_vocab_drugs']} vocabulary drugs are excluded as OOD equivalents; {len(rep['audit']['ood_drugs_with_equivalent_vocab_drug'])} OOD drugs have such an equivalent ({lst(rep['audit']['ood_drugs_with_equivalent_vocab_drug'])}) and all of them are in the sensitivity set below.")
