    L.append(f"- E7b, integrity control with fixed inputs: each passage is prefixed `source drug | section`, cut to a window of {320} characters centred on the first partner mention when there is one, and passages that name the partner are placed first; k = 5; own-label retrieval. Reachability R is the share of positives whose text, after the 512-token truncation, names the partner (partner synonyms by shared RxCUI). It was computed before any run on these exact inputs: R = {f3(rule['R_novel'])} for Novel and {f3(rule['R_older_primary'])} for Older-primary, and on the training pairs {f3(audit['e7b_train_reachability']['R_positives'])}. The assertion R >= {rule['R_floor']} {'holds' if rule['assertion_R_at_least_floor'] else 'FAILS'}. The pass threshold is T = max(0.75, 0.5 + 0.8 x (R - 0.5)): T = {f3(rule['threshold_novel'])} for Novel and {f3(rule['threshold_older_primary'])} for Older-primary. E7b passes if, on both Novel and Older-primary, the within-drug AUROC is at least T and its 95% lower bound is above {rule['lower_bound_floor']:.2f}. With the global contaminated retrieval of E7a the same fixed inputs reach only R = {f3(g('e7b_alt_fixed_global_contaminated','novel','novel','R_positives_with_partner_in_seen_text'))} (Novel) and {f3(g('e7b_alt_fixed_global_contaminated','older','older_primary','R_positives_with_partner_in_seen_text'))} (Older-primary), and literal partner matching there also fires on partner-label passages for {pct(g('e7b_alt_fixed_global_contaminated','novel','novel','negatives_with_partner_in_seen_text'))} of Novel negatives; that is why E7b uses own-label retrieval and E7a keeps the H5 retrieval.")
    L.append("- E7c names only, E7d other-labels retrieval, E7e clean retrieval (fixed input format as E7b): knowledge arms with no pass rule. Per arm and cohort the report gives the within-drug AUROC with its interval, kappa = (AUC - 0.5) / (AUC_DrugBank - 0.5) on the same rows, the training-label partner-prior scorer (smoothed positive rate of the partner in the training labels, `a7-prior-partner-train`), the label-free additive residual of `scripts/residual_analysis.py:49-56`, and paired differences between arms.")
    L.append(f"  - DrugBank lookup within-drug AUROC used for kappa, recomputed from the validation files: Novel {f3(db['novel']['novel'])}, Older-clean {f3(db['older']['older_clean'])}, Older-primary {f3(db['older']['older_primary'])}.")
    L.append("  - \"signal\": the partner-residualized within-drug AUROC has a 95% lower bound above 0.5 AND the paired difference against the training-label partner-prior scorer has a lower bound above 0. \"no signal\": the within-drug AUROC is equivalent to [0.40, 0.60] by two one-sided tests at 0.05 on Older-primary. Otherwise \"neither\".")
